        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In regards to some of the comments, one comments about avatars becoming bigger in size. I can already use the \"Infinite Gesture System\" demonstrated by Zeshin and add a crazy amount of items to my character. There are also ways to create animation \"point and activate\" on avatars so that you don't have to wait for some animation to get to where you want it with the infinite gesture system. So I'd say that the \"file size\" being a concern is already a moot point.\n\nNow, on the topic of the animation toggle, the animation toggle system is another way to add more items to an avatar like the two I mentioned above, but it is very limited in functionality. You can only have up to 8 different states whereas the above systems allow for a seemingly infinite number of states.\n\nThe big problem with all the above methods, however, is that avatar creators cannot change their hand gesture animations (well, I have a theory on how to do this one) and they can't easily change facial gestures. My gestures are used exclusively for facial gestures which means that I have a total of 7(?) different expressions that I can have on my face and if I want to change that for any reason, I would have to upload another version of my avatar with a different set of expressions and that version of my avatar may or may not benefit from future avatar work and development and will be left in the past.\n\nIf I had another menu/submenu (even if it sat in the corner of the emote menu and was only active if there were multiple gesture sets) that allowed me to toggle the animations for the hand gestures, that would help me out so much and I would only have to upload one avatar and I wouldn't have a need to switch just to change my facial expressions.\n\nWhat would you rather download in terms to file size? A few extra small animations that adjust shape keys, or 6-20 \"different\" avatars that all have just slightly different animations to change the facial expressions of the avatar?\n\nSince they'd be different avatars, you're looking at a 6-20x amount of data transfer vs a few extra kilabytes (less then 1 MB) of animations?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-01-24T17:12:19.796Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With this feature an avatar can hold up to 21 custom gestures and can easily switch them in a new tab in the quick menu called gesture modes. In this tab there will be 3 custom modes plus a default animation mode if you want to disable custom gestures on your own avatar. This will give avatar creators new ways to create avatars and I think this would be a great feature to add to VRChat.",
